.TH "TRCC\-LED" "1" "" "trcc\-linux 9.9.5" "TRCC Manual"
.SH NAME
trcc\-led \- RGB LED control
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrcc led\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
RGB LED control.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS brightness
.PP
\fBtrcc led brightness\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
.PP
Set the global LED brightness (persists).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBPERCENT\fR
Brightness 0\-100
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS clock\-format
.PP
\fBtrcc led clock\-format\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIFMT\fR
.PP
Set the 12h/24h clock display for LC2\-style segment devices.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBFMT\fR
\&'12h' or '24h'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS color
.PP
\fBtrcc led color\fR \fIKEY\fR \fICOLOR\fR
.PP
Set the LED color used by STATIC / BREATHING / COLORFUL modes.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBCOLOR\fR
Hex color (#rrggbb)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS disk\-index
.PP
\fBtrcc led disk\-index\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIINDEX\fR
.PP
Pick which disk's read/write stats to surface.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBINDEX\fR
Disk index (0\-based)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS initialize
.PP
\fBtrcc led initialize\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Connect + render one initial frame in a single dispatch. Convenience for boot scripts  \-  equivalent to device connect followed by led render, but in one Command so the caller only inspects one Result. Use this on app start; use the individual commands for finer control.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS list\-modes
.PP
\fBtrcc led list\-modes\fR
.PP
List every animation mode (STATIC, BREATHING, RAINBOW, ...).
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS list\-styles
.PP
\fBtrcc led list\-styles\fR
.PP
List every LED style registered in the PM byte registry.
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS load\-source
.PP
\fBtrcc led load\-source\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISOURCE\fR
.PP
Pick the sensor source for LOAD_LINKED mode.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBSOURCE\fR
\&'cpu' or 'gpu'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS memory\-ratio
.PP
\fBtrcc led memory\-ratio\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIRATIO\fR
.PP
Set the DDR memory multiplier for the LED memory gauge.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBRATIO\fR
DDR multiplier: 1, 2, or 4
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS mode
.PP
\fBtrcc led mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIMODE\fR
.PP
Set the LED animation mode (persists).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBMODE\fR
One of: static, breathing, colorful, rainbow, temp_linked, load_linked
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS play
.PP
\fBtrcc led play\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Run the LED render ticker until Ctrl\-C. Mirrors display play  \-  dispatches RenderLed every tick so BREATHING / COLORFUL / RAINBOW animations advance. Stops cleanly on SIGINT.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Tick interval in seconds (default: AppSettings.refresh_interval_s)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS render
.PP
\fBtrcc led render\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Render one LED frame from current settings + sensors and send. Reads the device's saved mode / color / brightness from Settings, advances the engine's phase counters on app.led_runtime, and sends one tick. Pass \-\-color to override the saved color (treated as STATIC at full brightness  \-  diagnostic shape).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-color, \-c \fICOLOR\fR\fR
Override hex color (#rrggbb); omit to use the saved color
.TP
\fB\-\-phase, \-p \fIPHASE\fR\fR
Rotation phase for multi\-phase displays
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS select\-zone
.PP
\fBtrcc led select\-zone\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIZONE\fR
.PP
Set the currently\-selected zone (UI state).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBZONE\fR
Zone index to select
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS set\-colors
.PP
\fBtrcc led set\-colors\fR \fIKEY\fR \fICOLORS\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Push a full LED color update.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBCOLORS\fR
Hex colors (#rrggbb), one per LED
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-brightness, \-b \fIBRIGHTNESS\fR\fR
Global brightness 0\-100
.TP
\fB\-\-off\fR
Force all LEDs off (overrides colors)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS snapshot
.PP
\fBtrcc led snapshot\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Print the persisted LED state for a device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON instead of human text.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS temp\-source
.PP
\fBtrcc led temp\-source\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISOURCE\fR
.PP
Pick the sensor source for TEMP_LINKED mode.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBSOURCE\fR
\&'cpu' or 'gpu'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS test\-led
.PP
\fBtrcc led test\-led\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Print an ANSI true\-color preview of the LED zones in the terminal. Reads the current zone color list from LedSnapshot and paints each zone as a coloured square  \-  handy for visualising multi\-zone strips during headless debugging.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS test\-mode
.PP
\fBtrcc led test\-mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fION\fR
.PP
Toggle the 4\-color diagnostic test cycle.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBON\fR
Enable (true) or disable (false)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS toggle
.PP
\fBtrcc led toggle\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Turn the LED device (or one zone) on/off.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' or 'off' (or use \-\-zone N to target one zone)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-zone, \-z \fIZONE\fR\fR
Toggle a single zone (omit for global toggle)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS toggle\-segment
.PP
\fBtrcc led toggle\-segment\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIINDEX\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Flip one segment on/off (segment\-display devices).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBINDEX\fR
Segment index
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' or 'off'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS week\-start
.PP
\fBtrcc led week\-start\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIDAY\fR
.PP
Pick the week\-start day on devices that show a day\-of\-week display.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBDAY\fR
\&'sunday' or 'monday'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS zone\-brightness
.PP
\fBtrcc led zone\-brightness\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIZONE\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
.PP
Set one zone's persistent brightness.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBZONE\fR
Zone index (0\-based)
.TP
\fBPERCENT\fR
Brightness 0\-100
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS zone\-color
.PP
\fBtrcc led zone\-color\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIZONE\fR \fICOLOR\fR
.PP
Set one zone's persistent color.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBZONE\fR
Zone index (0\-based)
.TP
\fBCOLOR\fR
Hex color (#rrggbb)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS zone\-mode
.PP
\fBtrcc led zone\-mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIZONE\fR \fIMODE\fR
.PP
Set one zone's persistent animation mode.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key, e.g. 0416:8001
.TP
\fBZONE\fR
Zone index (0\-based)
.TP
\fBMODE\fR
One of: static, breathing, colorful, rainbow, temp_linked, load_linked
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS zone\-sync
.PP
\fBtrcc led zone\-sync\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Toggle the zone\-sync carousel (optionally set the interval).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
LED device key
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' or 'off'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Set ticks\-per\-rotation alongside the toggle
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtrcc\fR(1)
